# What the Docker daemon receives as build context.
#
# The Dockerfile copies only pyproject.toml, README.md and src/, but the whole
# directory is uploaded first. Without this file that includes the git history,
# the local virtualenv and any generated synthetic corpus -- hundreds of
# megabytes, re-sent on every build.
#
# It is also a safety boundary, not only a speed one: anything in the context
# can be COPYed into an image by a future edit, and `.env` and `data/` are
# exactly the two things that must never end up in one.

.git
.gitattributes
.github

# Generated corpora and anything else gitignored under data/ (PHI-shaped even
# when synthetic -- it has no business inside an image).
data/

# Local environments and caches
.venv
venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov

# Secrets: .env is gitignored, so it is only ever local -- which is precisely
# why it would otherwise be swept into the context from a developer machine.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Node, for when the frontend arrives in M5
node_modules
frontend/dist

# Documentation and tests are not needed to run the service
docs/
tests/
tools/synthetic/
*.md
!README.md
